[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626728550","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113672#issuecomment-3626728550","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113672","id":3626728550,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YK3xm","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T12:37:14Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T12:37:14Z","body":"Can confirm, but with an error:\n```\nERROR: Parameter \"common_parent\" is null.\n   at: get_path_to (scene/main/node.cpp:2354)\nERROR: Condition \"!common_parent\" is true. Continuing.\n   at: _parse_connections (scene/resources/packed_scene.cpp:1208)\n```\nThe displayed connection goes away when the scene tab is switched or the scene is reloaded\n\nThis is an error probably in the decision of where to put the signal connection, it attempts to put it inside the saved scene but it should be in the parent scene\n\nThis also happens in 4.5.1 but there it keeps presenting the incorrect signal while the scene is open (in 4.6 it fixes the editor version directly, not sure what was changed there)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3626728550/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628680781","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113672#issuecomment-3628680781","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113672","id":3628680781,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YSUZN","user":{"login":"vilhalmer","id":201439,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTQzOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/201439?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer","html_url":"https://github.com/vilhalmer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilhalmer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-08T19:28:55Z","updated_at":"2025-12-08T19:41:15Z","body":"I can't provide anything close to a reliable reproduction, but I just ran into signals being mysteriously disconnected at runtime despite appearing in the editor and scene file. It fixed itself after I checked out an old version and then went back to the tip of my branch, restarting the editor at each commit. I suspect something must be getting stuck in the editor cache because there were no differences in the relevant scene file in the old commit. Attempting to delete the connection and recreate it in the UI also didn't fix it prior to checking out the old version.\n\nI'm on 4.5.1, but I also rolled back to 4.5 and it remained broken before the steps above so whatever it is must be persisted to disk somewhere. None of the above makes any sense to me since I am using remote deploy+debug and you'd think that would fix anything stuck in the local cache… so maybe it's something that only happens with the debugger attached?\n\nEdit: I should note I confirmed the signals were disconnected at runtime by adding a line just printing the result of `has_connections` since they don't yet appear in the node dock for remote nodes.\n\nEdit edit: I just remembered I saw the `common_parent` error a few days ago and couldn't figure out what it was related to. It hasn't appeared continuously though, just once.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628680781/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3628693767","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113672#issuecomment-3628693767","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113672","id":3628693767,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7YSXkH","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_